---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Initiative - TokenLens"
  description="Why we need TokenLens: transparent cost and context data for AI applications"
>
  <div class="initiative">
    <div class="container">
      <article class="content">
        <h1>The Initiative</h1>
        
        <section>
          <h2>Why TokenLens exists</h2>
          <p>
            AI applications need to make real-time decisions about model usage, context management, and cost control. 
            Yet most AI providers don't return transparent, structured cost and context data in their API responses.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>The Problem</h2>
          <p>
            When building AI applications, developers face critical questions on every API call:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Does this fit?</strong> Will my prompt exceed the model's context window?</li>
            <li><strong>What will it cost?</strong> How much am I spending per request, per conversation?</li>
            <li><strong>Should we compact now?</strong> When should I start removing old messages?</li>
            <li><strong>How much budget is left?</strong> Can I fit another turn in this conversation?</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Without structured metadata from providers, developers must:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Manually track and update model pricing across providers</li>
            <li>Remember context limits for dozens of models</li>
            <li>Parse different usage formats (OpenAI vs Anthropic vs others)</li>
            <li>Build custom solutions for cost estimation and context budgeting</li>
            <li>Hope their hardcoded values stay accurate as models change</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>What we need from providers</h2>
          <p>
            Imagine if every AI provider returned this in their API responses:
          </p>
          <pre><code>{`{
  "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
  "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 3200,
    "output_tokens": 400,
    "cost_usd": 0.00088
  },
  "limits": {
    "max_input_tokens": 128000,
    "max_output_tokens": 16384,
    "max_total_tokens": 128000
  }
}`}</code></pre>
          <p>
            With transparent cost and context metadata, developers could:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Track spending accurately without external tools</li>
            <li>Make informed decisions about context management</li>
            <li>Build better user experiences with token budgets</li>
            <li>Switch providers confidently knowing the real costs</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Until then, we have TokenLens</h2>
          <p>
            TokenLens provides what providers should: a canonical registry of model metadata, 
            usage normalization across SDKs, and utilities for cost estimation and context budgeting.
          </p>
          <p>
            It's SDK-agnostic, works great with the Vercel AI SDK, and stays up-to-date with 
            provider data from <a href="https://github.com/sst/models.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">models.dev</a> 
            and OpenRouter.
          </p>
          <p class="cta">
            We built TokenLens because <strong>developers shouldn't have to guess</strong>. They should <strong>know</strong>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Join the movement</h2>
          <p>
            If you believe AI providers should return transparent cost and context data, 
            share this page and star the project on <a href="https://github.com/xn1cklas/tokenlens" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Together, we can push for better standards in AI API design.
          </p>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .initiative {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 750px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.75rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  section {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
  }

  ul {
    margin: 1rem 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: hsl(var(--muted-foreground));
  }

  strong {
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  a {
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }

  a:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }

  pre {
    background: hsl(var(--muted));
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  code {
    font-family: "Monaco", "Courier New", monospace;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .cta {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .initiative {
      padding: 2rem 0;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>

